fuzzing	`cargo-fuzz` (libFuzzer) targets for every parser of	targets nfr-03, fuzz targets nfr-03, nfr-03, cargo-fuzz libfuzzer targets, targets, file, whole, fuzz
overview	Your skills, code patterns, manuals and project notes go into one `.kapu` file. The agent first sees a map of every section with its token price, searches, and opens only the sections it needs. Nothing to host: one binary, an optional offline embedding model, and a plain UTF-8 file you can copy anywhere. It is built for two cases: **coding agents** that should use your accumulated knowledge on any platform, and **local LLMs**, where every token in the context costs memory and seconds. Every reply of the MCP server starts with its own price in tokens and stays within a budget the agent sets. **1. Install** the prebuilt `kapu` and `kapu-mcp` (Windows x64, Linux x64, macOS on Apple silicon), with the embedding model included. No Rust, no Python. The scripts download the archive of the latest release, check its SHA-256, unpack it under your user folder and print the next commands. You can also download the archive from [Releases](https://github.com/piszabolcs/kapu/releases) yourself. **2. Pack** a folder of agent skills, or any folder of Markdown files (one room per file, `##` headings become sections): **3. Connect** it to Claude Code (other clients: [Connect an	kapu, kapu file, file, one kapu file, agent, one, skills, results
